1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,340
Oh, no, Mikoy! You're not allowed to look!

2
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,258
It's bad luck!

3
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:54,888
<i>As soon as I get any information</i>

4
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:59,476
that says there's a threat or danger
to Mikoy and Chiara's lives,

5
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,978
you'll be the very first to know.

6
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,688
Thank you, my friend.

7
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,106
<i>I trust your words.</i>

8
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,822
Here it is, right?

9
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:14,407
<i>We're almost there.</i>

10
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:16,785
We'll officially be in-laws soon.

11
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,329
<i>Thank you, in-law.</i>

12
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,873
For being there for Chiara.

13
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,833
<i>Thank you for taking care of her.</i>

14
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,508
Hey, Carlota.

15
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:33,384
What are you doing here?

16
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:35,762
Waiting for you.

17
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:38,014
Okay, sure. Shall we?

18
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:38,973
Shall we?

19
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:45,355
Sorry, Sweet won't be able to make it.

20
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:48,691
So I'm here instead. I'm her father.

21
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:51,945
James?

22
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:56,991
Tailor.

23
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,493
James Tailor.

24
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,744
James Tailor.

25
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:02,622
It's a pleasure to be here.

26
00:02:02,705 --> 00:02:04,624
- Pleased to meet you.
- Hello, sir.

27
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:07,627
This one's yours.

28
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:10,547
Try it on.

29
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,506
Looks good.

30
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,049
- Thank you.
- All right.

31
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,759
- It suits you, Mikoy.
- There. Go, go, go.

32
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:19,097
- Where's mine?
- This one's mine.

33
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:20,807
Wow.

34
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,684
- This one's mine.
- All right.

35
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:26,771
Good grief!

36
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:28,022
What's that, Jan-Jan?

37
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,816
- What's wrong?
- Why does something seem off?

38
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:31,484
It really is wrong.

39
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,069
Mr. James.

40
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:34,445
- Something seems wrong.
- What's your name?

41
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:36,239
- Jan-jan, sir.
- Jan-Jan.

42
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:39,075
Oh, no!

43
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:42,662
Let's change that, Jan-Jan.

44
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,123
I'm a man.

45
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,960
- Does it fit?
- This one's nice.

46
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:49,752
Jan-Jan.

47
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,546
- This one suits you.
- How about this one?

48
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:52,463
Does it look okay?

49
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:53,298
Hey.

50
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:55,717
Why does it look… James, why is it loose?

51
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:57,635
The fit isn't right.

52
00:02:58,136 --> 00:03:00,221
- Sorry, sorry.
- What happened? Why is it like that?

53
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:03,516
Wait, Tailor Sweet said the fitting
was supposed to be perfect, right?

54
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,852
- What happened?
- Yes, I was the one who recommended them.

55
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,562
Mikoy, I think you lost weight.

56
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:09,856
Have you been drinking slimming tea?

57
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,608
No, sir.

58
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:13,860
Then why is that?

59
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,030
No, sir.

60
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:20,867
Did you… Did you crash diet?

61
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:25,872
- You went on a crash diet?
- I tried going on a diet,

62
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:28,458
but I gave up right away.

63
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,169
Maybe… Wait.

64
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:32,837
Hold on.

65
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:36,507
Measure him again.

66
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:39,177
Brother Mikoy, I think
you've been stressed.

67
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,929
Stress really makes you lose weight.

68
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:42,305
Yes, I guess so.

69
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:44,057
It's really been stressful.

70
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,893
The past few days
have been pretty stressful too.

71
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,896
So that's how it works.

72
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:53,441
No wonder I don't lose weight easily.
I don't get stressed that fast.

73
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:57,570
That's why, buddy Mikoy,
let's pig out later.

74
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:59,030
- Hey.
- To avoid stress.

75
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:02,116
Dekyo, what if my stomach gets
as big as yours?

76
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,451
Then it'll look awful.

77
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:05,745
You're really something, Dekyo.

78
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:08,373
That'll just stress Mikoy out even more.

79
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:11,668
Wait, wait. What are you stressing about?

80
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,753
Everything's already taken care of.

81
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:16,214
Except for what you're going to wear.

82
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:19,092
Exactly.

83
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:21,594
I'm worried about Chiara.

84
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:24,681
She might get stressed if she finds out
my barong doesn't fit perfectly.

85
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:27,976
- Oh, no.
- You know, when it comes to our wedding,

86
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:30,436
I just want her to be
the happiest she can be.

87
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:33,982
This is so much fun.

88
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:39,946
Of course. We girls deserve this, right?

89
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:43,283
We deserve to relax from time to time.

90
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:46,786
It's such a shame Mom isn't here.

91
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,872
This is our favorite way to bond.

92
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,333
Aside from shopping, of course.

93
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:56,629
When it comes to any kind of pampering,
we're always on the same page.

94
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:59,590
Are you okay, sweetheart?

95
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,552
I'm okay, Mom.

96
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:08,891
I just miss Mom, but I'm happy
because you're both here for me.

97
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:11,227
I really appreciate you both.

98
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:16,566
You know, personally,

99
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:18,443
I'm happy to spend time
with you two as well.

100
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:21,070
And you know, coming here to Albay

101
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:23,072
is a stress reliever for me too.

102
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:25,325
And sweetheart, you know,

103
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:29,370
I understand that you want
your wedding day to be perfect, right?

104
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,290
But you need to chill a little,

105
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,500
so you can let go of those nerves.

106
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,919
- Being a bridezilla doesn't suit you.
- That's right.

107
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:38,629
You're right, Mom.

108
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:42,425
It's just that I really thought
wedding planning would be easy.

109
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:43,968
I even said before,

110
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:46,429
"Logistics? Easy.

111
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:50,266
Event planning? Piece of cake."

112
00:05:50,349 --> 00:05:54,812
I don't know. Lately,
my hormones are just… up and down.

113
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,939
I don't understand what's happening.

114
00:05:57,023 --> 00:06:00,693
It's like I'm worried
about every single thing.

115
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:02,445
Oh, Chiara. That's normal.

116
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:05,114
You're not preparing
for just any simple event.

117
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:08,284
You're welcoming a new chapter
in your life as a woman.

118
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,411
So a lot of things are going
to change in your life,

119
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,538
which is why you're bound
to have mixed emotions.

120
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:16,125
You know, when I was getting married,

121
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,960
I was incredibly nervous too.

122
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:20,254
I couldn't sit still,
and I got emotional too,

123
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:22,507
so what you're going through
is completely normal.

124
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:26,636
You know, sweetheart, what's important
is we're all here together for you.

125
00:06:26,719 --> 00:06:27,720
Right?

126
00:06:28,846 --> 00:06:33,726
That's really how it is when you know
the wedding is just around the corner.

127
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:37,522
That's when all these challenges
start piling up one after another.

128
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,192
It seems like the two of you
are on a pledge

129
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:43,402
and put your relationship to the test.

130
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,321
That's so true, Mr. James.

131
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:47,824
As the wedding gets closer,

132
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:50,034
you should grow stronger
through challenges like this.

133
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:52,078
Your love for each other
should grow even stronger.

134
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:53,037
Right.

135
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:55,248
That's how it goes.

136
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:57,959
But you can handle the adjustments, right?

137
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,378
You can handle them, Mikoy.

138
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,880
Just don't let yourself
get too stressed out.

139
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,006
- See?
- That's right.

140
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:08,845
Eat properly, get enough sleep,
and when the time comes,

141
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:12,140
don't go drinking, okay?

142
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:14,058
Save it for after the wedding.

143
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,977
We'll do it at the reception!

144
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,520
- Correct.
- Right!

145
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:21,649
So for now,
we'll just pretend we're drinking.

146
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:23,025
Let's just pretend for now.

147
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,194
- All right.
- Just pretend.

148
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,364
So your barong will fit perfectly
and be tailored just right.

149
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,574
Right?

150
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:30,908
So, cheers!

151
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:35,413
To Mikoy, and may he
not get stressed over the wedding!

152
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:39,584
And to a hassle-free
and stress-free wedding for us!

153
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:46,174
- This is strong. No chaser?
- This is really strong.

154
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:48,968
I want more.

155
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:56,434
Mikoy. Are you okay?

156
00:07:57,727 --> 00:07:58,853
Yes.

157
00:07:58,936 --> 00:08:00,688
No, I was just thinking that,

158
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:03,774
you know, it would probably be more fun
if my best man were here.

159
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:05,276
Angelito.

160
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:07,153
Why don't you video call him?

161
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:09,363
So he can get excited about what
you'll be wearing at the wedding too.

162
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:10,406
No, it's okay.

163
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:13,201
Besides, he should be
in class at this hour.

164
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:15,161
I might just disturb him.

165
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:18,915
I really can't help but miss my brother.

166
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:20,333
Bro Mikoy.

167
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:22,960
I've got you. Don't worry.

168
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:25,171
Once we get your bachelor party arranged,

169
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,840
all the grooms will be there.

170
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,760
- Angelito will be there with us.
- Angelito.

171
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:32,261
We'll all hang out together.

172
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:33,638
We'll all be together!

173
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:35,765
There you go!

174
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:37,099
That's what I've been waiting for!

175
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,060
Your bachelor party.

176
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:39,977
Exciting.

177
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,522
- My goodness.
- Are you paying for it?

178
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:43,648
No!

179
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:47,360
I'm excited about the fun
we're going to have with Bro Mikoy!

180
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:50,488
There you go again
with that bachelor party.

181
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:51,822
Take it easy, guys.

182
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:54,742
We can have fun,
as long as we don't get into trouble.

183
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:56,827
- Yes, that's right.
- Trouble, trouble.

184
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:57,995
Bro Mikoy.

185
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,247
You said trouble?

186
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:00,164
Oh, no!

187
00:09:01,123 --> 00:09:02,875
We're definitely not getting into trouble.

188
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:03,793
I've got this.

189
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:07,213
That's right, that's right.
And don't overthink things, Mikoy.

190
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:09,882
Because I don't want
my Brother Mikoy to get stressed.

191
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:13,636
- Careful, you're spilling my drink.
- Sorry.

192
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:16,055
- Cheers!
- Let's cheers!

193
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:20,601
- We haven't had anything like this before.
- Hello?

194
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:22,728
Dad, where are you?

195
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:24,313
Uncle James is here.

196
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:25,898
Your barong is ready.

197
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,152
- Looking sharp.
- You're the one looking sharp.

198
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,446
We're all here for you.

199
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,949
Thank you so much, really.

200
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:38,327
Because of that, we need to enjoy this.

201
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,538
This ultimate pamper day of ours.

202
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:42,707
- Yes.
- We deserve this, ladies.

203
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,126
- Come on, it should be guilt-free!
- I'm so excited!

204
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:48,045
It's been so long
since I treated myself like this.

205
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,922
Help me with this.

206
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:51,299
There you go.

207
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:54,969
Just a moment, okay?

208
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,429
Take your time.

209
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:03,811
Do you know how rarely I get a foot spa?

210
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:09,609
<i>But believe me.</i>
<i>This call is about an urgent matter.</i>

211
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:14,405
I have an update on the video
and the mysterious vigilante.

212
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,950
All right, I'm listening.

213
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:21,912
Unfortunately, we still haven't identified
the person in the video.

214
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:25,666
<i>There are just too many factors</i>
<i>to consider.</i>

215
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:30,504
<i>His age, gender,</i>
<i>background, and nationality.</i>

216
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:35,718
Here's what I noticed.

217
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:38,346
<i>The way he moves isn't ordinary.</i>

218
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,183
But it's not military training.

219
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,477
If it's not military training,
then what is it?

220
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,566
Like Chiara's.

221
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:54,278
Huh?! Are you sure about that?

222
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,990
You're awfully quick to conclude
that his style comes from elite training.

223
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,700
<i>I'm sure.</i>

224
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:02,620
<i>I made sure of this information</i>
<i>before I called you.</i>

225
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:07,958
I think this mysterious vigilante
is of a different nationality.

226
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:11,545
Like Donatello?

227
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:13,547
The one I met in Hong Kong.

228
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,259
Wait, are you saying

229
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:20,054
there's an assassin invited
to Chiara's wedding?

230
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:23,724
There are barely any guests
coming from the bride's side.

231
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:28,020
Just me, and possibly Donabel and Viktor
if their request is granted.

232
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:31,565
Well, if he's not invited,

233
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:34,610
maybe he's the uninvited wedding guest?

234
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,779
That can't be.

235
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:39,532
It wouldn't be good to have a surprise
guest with assassin-style training

236
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:41,575
showing up at your wedding.

237
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:45,121
But could Chiara still have
unfinished business with La Concordat?

238
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:47,373
<i>Could someone be trying</i>
<i>to get in touch with her?</i>

239
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:49,500
I don't think it's La Concordat.

240
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:50,918
Ever since La Morte Bianca was killed,

241
00:11:51,001 --> 00:11:53,337
they've slowed down their operations.

242
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:55,756
Who is that vigilante, anyway?

243
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:58,717
And even if he's assassin-trained,

244
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:01,762
this is going to be way too stressful
for Mikoy and Chiara.

245
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:06,434
No, no, no. It's okay.

246
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:08,561
I'm the one who taught you
to be overprepared

247
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:10,354
and overreact when necessary.

248
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:13,357
<i>As agents, we can't afford</i>
<i>to let our guard down.</i>

249
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,527
Better dig deeper, Agent Dara.

250
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:20,781
If you truly believe this vigilante
has elite training,

251
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:24,285
then we should probably go through
recent foreign entries

252
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,412
from the past one or two months.

253
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:28,497
Then let's check if any of them
have a similar background.

254
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:36,255
It fits.

255
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:37,756
This fits really well.

256
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,384
Sir Mario!

257
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:43,429
Dad really is so handsome!

258
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,806
Of course. There's no one
more blessed and handsome than me.

259
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,683
There!

260
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:48,976
Probably just me.

261
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:50,227
What about you?

262
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:52,229
There's still time.

263
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,939
James can still make adjustments.

264
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:58,360
Okay, but what's important
is that you know we're all here

265
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,696
to help you and Chiara.

266
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:04,492
Everything will work out.

267
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:06,952
Thanks, Dad.

268
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,666
Why, Dad?

269
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,544
Are you okay?

270
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,218
I just had a flashback.

271
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:25,888
I just remembered when you were still

272
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:28,516
a little boy.

273
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,645
Now you're about to have
a family of your own.

274
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,066
Time really flies, son.

275
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:44,782
I'm happy for you. Don't get me wrong.

276
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:49,828
But you can't blame me

277
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,414
if I get a little sentimental.

278
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,131
Oh?

279
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,466
Are you okay?

280
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,887
Of course, Dad.

281
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,430
I'm perfectly fine.

282
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:12,518
And you know, no one from Pinagpala
is ever too manly to get sentimental.

283
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:14,270
There's nothing wrong with that!

284
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:16,021
Even if you are feeling sentimental.

285
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,108
Every man gets sentimental
at one time or another.

286
00:14:19,191 --> 00:14:21,527
You're right, Dad.

287
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:22,736
It's actually healthy,

288
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,281
because we're letting out
everything we're feeling, right?

289
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,115
Yes.

290
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:29,243
And with that, group hug!

291
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:35,541
- Yes, boy!
- Nice.

292
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:37,626
You know, Sir Mario,

293
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,461
you just gave me an idea.

294
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:44,049
I think you should be my guest
on my livestream later.

295
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,467
Oh, there.

296
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:46,510
Me?

297
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,515
What am I supposed to do there?

298
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,894
Eat a lot? No, I'll just choke.

299
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,854
No, Sir Mario, don't worry.

300
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:58,188
We're not doing a mukbang.

301
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:00,608
We're just gonna hang out.

302
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:08,490
Just like that.

303
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:11,327
You're a grown man,
and you're calling it a crib.

304
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:14,538
It's not an actual crib, Sir Mario.

305
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:17,583
It's just slang.

306
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:22,046
It means we're
just hanging out at our house.

307
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:24,298
Right? What you think?

308
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:25,591
Sir Mario, G?

309
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:27,551
- G?
- What's "G"?

310
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:29,929
Is that how it works?

311
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:30,888
Yes.

312
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,474
Game, like, like <i>"Game ka na ba?"</i>

313
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:36,810
I'm totally game!

314
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:39,939
G all the way!

315
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,357
Sir Mario!

316
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,610
Mario, Captain wants to see you.

317
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,820
Right now? Why? Did something happen?

318
00:15:46,904 --> 00:15:49,198
An update about the Manananggal?

319
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:50,991
- Manananggal?
- Manananggal?

320
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:53,953
Tell him I'll just get changed,

321
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:56,080
then I'll head over to the barangay hall.

322
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:57,122
Okay, sir.

323
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,999
Manananggal?

324
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:01,919
And that was sudden.

325
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,087
That's right.

326
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:30,614
<i>Who were you talking to earlier?</i>

327
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:33,575
<i>What are you hiding, Sianong?</i>

328
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:37,705
<i>And why am I only seeing</i>
<i>these red flags now?</i>

329
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:51,051
Oh, wow.

330
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:53,637
We're already halfway through the year,

331
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:57,182
and I'm still so far
from reaching my glow-up goals.

332
00:16:57,891 --> 00:16:59,977
So this is what it's like
to be in your thirties.

333
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,895
Your metabolism isn't as fast anymore.

334
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:05,607
Exactly. That's why when it comes
to fitness goals,

335
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:09,194
you have to set realistic expectations.

336
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:12,197
When it comes to fitness
and your health, you can't rush it.

337
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,490
True.

338
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:16,452
I only started working out last week.

339
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,537
Well, that explains it.

340
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,581
It doesn't happen overnight, right?

341
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:23,042
You have to… You know, after a year,

342
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,376
you have to stay consistent.

343
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,837
That's when you'll start
seeing the changes.

344
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:31,425
All right, glow-up coming soon.

345
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:38,307
Sorry to disturb your glow-up goals talk.

346
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:41,435
But did you know Viktor
was transferred to another prison?

347
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:43,270
Huh? When did that happen?

348
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:45,481
They didn't report it to me.

349
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:47,274
I only found out just now.

350
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:50,527
But it looks like they transferred him
the other night.

351
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:53,197
To the most secluded area,

352
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:56,408
and Viktor was transferred
to maximum security.

353
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:10,339
Maybe you could ask them

354
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,883
to put us back under house arrest.

355
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:15,385
I promise I'll work even harder.

356
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,054
Just don't keep us here.

357
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:18,639
I'm scared to death.

358
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,726
Chiara was right about you, Brusko.

359
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,479
You really are a scaredy-cat.

360
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:32,653
Come on, Sir Viktor.

361
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,696
Of course we're scared.

362
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,074
We're locked up in here.

363
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:40,077
We can do something when we're outside.
That's when I can be Brusko.

364
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,128
Could it be that

365
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:53,090
Viktor committed a serious violation
inside the safehouse?

366
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:55,968
That's why they transferred him
so quickly?

367
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:57,719
That's possible.

368
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:02,850
But for high-profile cases like Moraviano,

369
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:06,937
they need a judge's approval
before transferring them.

370
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:09,064
And in a regular prison,

371
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,692
the level of threat against them is high.

372
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:16,488
And with his years of experience
in the Mafia world,

373
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,699
everything he knows is valuable.

374
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,786
Could someone be targeting him?

375
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:25,914
And who could his enemy be?

376
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,208
La Morte Bianca is dead,

377
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:31,670
and the Concordat
has slowed down its operations.

378
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:36,258
And the Sinigang cartel is gone too.

379
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:40,387
Now, Ben, that's where you're wrong.
What you think is gone

380
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:42,222
is still around.

381
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:49,855
I'm wrong?

382
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:52,608
That doesn't happen very often to me.

383
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:56,904
Besides being born handsome,
I was also born always being right.

384
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:58,989
You know, Ben,

385
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:01,366
- you were actually right!
- Right.

386
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:03,619
But you know, I heard that

387
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:07,915
Agent Alex is supposedly coming
to the office today.

388
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,333
Alex!

389
00:20:09,416 --> 00:20:10,459
My TOTGA!

390
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,420
Hurry, check the parking lot.

391
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:18,383
Maybe she's already carrying
her gift for you from Albay!

392
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:22,387
- Go!
- All right.

393
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,473
- Your hair, your hair.
- Bye!

394
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:27,059
What's that about?

395
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:30,979
You almost slipped up
about Senator Quintin.

396
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,982
Sorry, I got carried away.

397
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:40,113
You criminals sure do talk a lot.

398
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:43,909
Let's see now if you can still chat.

399
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:46,036
Boss, just relax.

400
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:50,165
This guy is from Prague, huh?

401
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,083
Go on, go on.

402
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:53,210
Let's teach him a lesson.

403
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:55,337
Boss, that's enough.

404
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:00,884
Don't, Brusko.

405
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,303
You don't have to do this anymore.

406
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:07,683
I'll take it all!

407
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:23,240
Rahmboy, how have you been?

408
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:27,452
Why are you so quiet?

409
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:28,954
Is something wrong?

410
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:29,913
Yes.

411
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,165
You seem down.

412
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:34,001
Did you get bashed online?

413
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:36,169
Nothing's wrong.

414
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:37,754
Mama Tess.

415
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:41,383
No one's bashing me either, Sir Mario.

416
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,012
I'm just worried about something.

417
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:51,059
Oh, he remembered something,
probably because of what we're eating.

418
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:54,021
I got it.

419
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:59,109
Maybe Rahmboy has a crush
on a girl who loves rice cakes.

420
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,448
I'm not worried about a crush.

421
00:22:05,782 --> 00:22:06,950
Who is it?

422
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:08,618
My mom.

423
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:15,375
This biko is her favorite.

424
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:17,210
Oh, it's your mom.

425
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:20,380
So what happened to your mom?

426
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,632
I heard she went abroad to work, right?

427
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:23,592
Yes.

428
00:22:25,427 --> 00:22:27,429
I was still young when she left.

429
00:22:27,929 --> 00:22:31,058
It's been so long
since we last saw each other.

430
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:35,687
She said I should
get used to us being apart.

431
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:40,650
But sometimes, you just can't help it.

432
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:43,361
And sometimes,

433
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:47,074
the sadness just hits you.

434
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,328
You know that feeling when

435
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:54,998
you miss your mom so much.

436
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:07,135
Rahmboy.

437
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:10,222
That's completely normal.

438
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:13,183
Of course, that's your mother.

439
00:23:13,266 --> 00:23:15,685
You're bound to miss her.

440
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:18,939
Oh, dear.

441
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:22,025
The sacrifices of OFWs

442
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:25,529
and the families they leave behind
here in the Philippines.

443
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:29,616
Don't worry, Rahmboy.

444
00:23:29,699 --> 00:23:31,868
Just a little longer.

445
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,286
Hang in there.

446
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:39,084
All those years you've spent apart
from your family will be worth it.

447
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:46,091
And while you can't share some kakanin
with your mom just yet,

448
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:49,678
you have me, Mommy Tess,
and Dad Mario here with you.

449
00:23:55,475 --> 00:23:57,352
Okay, I'm really okay.

450
00:23:57,435 --> 00:23:58,770
There, he's happy again.

451
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:00,313
Can you hand me that?

452
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:01,690
So you can eat.

453
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:03,400
How are you going to use this?

454
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:05,735
Rahmboy.

455
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:06,695
Yes?

456
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:08,822
Could I ask you a favor?

457
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:10,073
Could you get from the fridge

458
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,783
the calamansi juice I made?

459
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:14,494
It'll go well
with what we're eating, right?

460
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:17,330
And while you're at it,
get me some extra ice too.

461
00:24:17,414 --> 00:24:19,791
- Okay? To keep it cold. Go on.
- That's exactly what I'm saying.

462
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:21,376
I'll get some ice.

463
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:23,086
- There you go.
- Don't forget, okay?

464
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,057
I don't think I've seen her
around here before.

465
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:37,601
Us neither.

466
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:38,810
She looks like an outsider.

467
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:40,854
Looks like she came from abroad.

468
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:43,857
Maybe she's attending the wedding.

469
00:24:45,358 --> 00:24:48,486
- Yes.
- We only invited a few people.

470
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:50,780
And she's not even related to me.

471
00:24:51,781 --> 00:24:53,825
Maybe she's from Chiara's side.

472
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:55,368
No.

473
00:24:55,452 --> 00:24:57,579
She didn't mention anything to me.

474
00:24:59,706 --> 00:25:02,000
And you know Chiara and I only wanted
our closest friends and family

475
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:04,294
to be invited to the wedding.

476
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:10,926
Mom!

477
00:25:12,969 --> 00:25:17,182
Didn't we just talk about
how much he misses his mom?

478
00:25:17,265 --> 00:25:19,726
And now, suddenly, it's a reunion!

479
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:22,729
I'm so happy for Rahmboy, aren't you?

480
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:12,404
My dear.

481
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:24,624
You guys take care of our guests.

482
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:26,334
Perfect!

483
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:28,128
- Are you Viktor?
- Relax, boss!

484
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,755
Senator wants us to welcome you.

485
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:37,137
But wouldn't going after Viktor
put Senator Quintin's ties

486
00:26:37,220 --> 00:26:40,473
to the Sinigang Cartel at risk?

487
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:43,768
Unless he has other plans for Viktor.

488
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:45,937
What you were saying is not impossible.

489
00:26:48,982 --> 00:26:50,734
- Huh?
- There's someone back there.

490
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:51,693
- Where?
- They're wearing black!

491
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:52,694
- Huh?!
- There they are!

492
00:26:52,777 --> 00:26:54,279
- Bro! Bro! Wait!
- Just come with us, bro!

493
00:26:54,362 --> 00:26:55,655
- Do not resist.
- Bro!

494
00:26:55,739 --> 00:26:56,990
- Mom!
- Quit fighting!

495
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:59,117
Mom! Dad!

496
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,285
Okay, okay, okay!

497
00:27:02,746 --> 00:27:04,581
Sounds like a success!

498
00:27:05,081 --> 00:27:06,499
Enjoy, Brother Mikoy!
